      Shown ONLY when the tap-and-hold selection breaks the rule (exactly one
      action). Deliberately not a permanent hint: the sheet stays quiet until it has
      something to say.
    -->
    <string name="gesture_hold_rule">1 option selected. Touching and holding will not switch modes.</string>

    <!--
      The status line, and it must stay TRUE. It used to say the selections were
      stored on the phone only, because the `function` enum was unknown; that is no
      longer the case, so leaving it would be a plain lie on screen. The `function`
      bytes are now measured (see GestureAction) and a change IS written to the buds.
      UPDATED 2026-09-22: the second sentence used to say the buds alone decide which
      modes the hold's ANC cycle contains. That was true only because the mask write
      was not wired yet — it now is (see GestureAction.holdMaskBit, PROTOCOL.md §5), so
      the sentence would be a lie again if left as it was.
    -->
    <string name="gesture_write_note">Changes are sent to the earbuds, then read back to confirm.</string>

